      "content": "Your caution about feeling overwhelmed and concerned about your appetite are completely understandable. However, it's very important to remember that even small amounts of tyramine can pose serious health risks when taking an MAOI. These medications can cause abrupt increases in blood pressure, which can be dangerous and even life-threatening. The risks associated with MAOI medication are not minor and cannot be mitigated by consuming these foods sparingly. It's important to establish a consistent, safe eating pattern and work closely with your healthcare professionals to find ways to keep your diet balanced and something you can adhere to long-term. Your well-being and safety are the top priority.",
      "source": "target",
